{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>You have heard.</b> What you have heard, see — all of it has come." "<b>And you, will you not declare?</b> For so it is; behold, I have made you hear new things from now." "<b>and guarded.</b> That they are guarded, and the meaning is with HaShem."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {0 "Reading ראה as imperative addressed to the prophet."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:30.541310382Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}